{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs22\b\qc PhilHealth Enrollment and Benefit Access Support Program\b0\par\par\b Project Objective:\b0 Improve access to PhilHealth benefits and affordable healthcare among target households\par\b Target Beneficiaries:\b0 Uninsured and underinsured households in [area]\par\b Duration:\b0 [12-24 months]\par\b Geographic Coverage:\b0 [district/city/province]\par\par\trowd\trgaph108\trleft-108\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdro\brdrs \cellx1920\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdro\brdrs \cellx5515\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdro\brdrs \cellx7665\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdro\brdrs \cellx10040\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdro\brdrs \cellx12090\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdro\brdrs \pard\intbl\b Level\b0\cell\b Narrative Summary\b0\cell\b Indicators\b0\cell\b Means of Verification\b0\cell\b Assumptions / Risks\b0\cell\row\pard\intbl Goal\cell Improved access to affordable, equitable, and timely healthcare services for target communities through PhilHealth coverage and benefit utilization\cell - % of target population with active PhilHealth membership\par- Reduction in out-of-pocket healthcare spending\par- Increase in utilization of covered services\cell Household surveys; PhilHealth membership registry; facility records; financial records\cell Assumption: Government and local health systems remain functional\parRisk: Policy changes, weak local coordination, funding constraints\cell\row\pard\intbl Outcome 1\cell Increased enrollment and retention of eligible households in PhilHealth\cell - % of eligible households enrolled in PhilHealth\par- % of enrolled members retaining active status\par- Number of newly enrolled members\cell Enrollment records; PhilHealth reports; monitoring reports\cell Assumption: Beneficiaries are eligible and willing to enroll\parRisk: Low awareness, low trust, administrative delays\cell\row\pard\intbl Outcome 2\cell Improved utilization of PhilHealth benefits among target members\cell - % of enrolled members using services covered by PhilHealth\par- Average number of claims submitted per month\par- % of beneficiaries receiving reimbursements/benefits\cell Claims data; facility records; PhilHealth benefit reports\cell Assumption: Accredited facilities remain operational\parRisk: Delayed claims processing, low provider compliance\cell\row\pard\intbl Outcome 3\cell Improved quality and accessibility of health services for PhilHealth members\cell - Average waiting time at facilities\par- Patient satisfaction rate\par- % of referrals completed on time\cell Facility service records; patient surveys; referral logs\cell Assumption: Service providers remain available and responsive\parRisk: Staff shortages, supply issues\cell\row\pard\intbl Output 1\cell Community awareness of PhilHealth benefits increased\cell - Number of community education sessions conducted\par- Number of participants reached\par- % of target households aware of PhilHealth benefits\cell Attendance sheets; session reports; pre/post awareness surveys\cell Assumption: Community mobilizers and local leaders are available\parRisk: Low turnout, poor information dissemination\cell\row\pard\intbl Output 2\cell Enrollment support provided to eligible households\cell - Number of households assisted with registration\par- % of assisted households successfully enrolled\par- Number of beneficiaries receiving direct support\cell Enrollment forms; support logs; PhilHealth enrollment reports\cell Assumption: Registration systems and local support staff are functioning\parRisk: Bureaucratic delays, incomplete documentation\cell\row\pard\intbl Output 3\cell Facility staff trained on PhilHealth claims and benefit processing\cell - Number of staff trained\par- % of facilities with trained personnel\par- % of claims processed within target timeframe\cell Training attendance sheets; training reports; claims processing reports\cell Assumption: Staff are available for training and retention\parRisk: Staff turnover, limited capacity\cell\row\pard\intbl Output 4\cell Referral and coordination mechanisms strengthened\cell - Number of referrals made\par- Referral completion rate\par- Number of facility coordination meetings conducted\cell Referral logs; meeting minutes; monitoring reports\cell Assumption: Referral pathways are in place and functioning\parRisk: Lack of coordination or transport barriers\cell\row\pard\intbl Output 5\cell Beneficiary monitoring and program reporting improved\cell - % of facilities submitting monthly reports\par- % of indicators tracked on schedule\par- Number of monitoring visits conducted\cell Monitoring reports; dashboards; monthly review meetings\cell Assumption: Data systems and reporting schedules are functioning\parRisk: Incomplete reports, weak data quality\cell\row\pard\intbl Activities\cell 1. Conduct community orientation and education on PhilHealth benefits\par2. Support registration and renewal of eligible members\par3. Train facility and administrative staff on PhilHealth processes\par4. Strengthen referral pathways and coordinate case management\par5. Monitor enrollment, claims, and service use and address bottlenecks\cell - Number of education sessions delivered\par- Number of households assisted\par- Number of staff trained\par- Number of monitoring visits conducted\cell Activity reports; training records; monitoring logs; attendance sheets\cell Assumption: Roles and responsibilities are clearly assigned\parRisk: Delays in implementation, inadequate staffing, limited funding\cell\row\pard\par\par\b Key Assumptions:\b0\par- Eligible households are willing to register and renew membership\par- Facilities remain accredited and operational\par- PhilHealth data systems and reporting processes remain available\par- Local government and partner agencies provide support\par\par\b Key Risks and Mitigation:\b0\par- Low awareness of benefits -> Community outreach and IEC campaign\par- Delayed claims processing -> Staff training and monitoring of claims turnaround\par- Low enrollment among target groups -> Direct enrollment support and targeted outreach\par- Provider noncompliance -> Regular performance review and coordination\par- Funding or logistics constraints -> Budget tracking and contingency planning\par}